<title>MALAYSIA: CRICKET-SCOTLAND BEAT IRELAND IN ICC TROPHY PLAYOFF.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SCOTLAND BEAT IRELAND IN ICC TROPHY PLAYOFF.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scotland beat Ireland by 46 runs on Friday in the third-place playoff of the International Cricket Council Trophy in a match reduced to 45 overs because of rain.</p>
<p>Scores: Scotland 187-8 in 45 overs (Mike Smith 49), Ireland 141 all out in 39 overs (Keith Sheridan 4-34).</p>
<p>Scotland qualify for the World Cup finals to be held in England in 1999.</p>
</text>
